# SAMPLE-set-template.def.in — template for the .def files webwork-build writes
#
# To use: copy this file to set-template.def.in in the course's WeBWorK directory
# (WEBWORK/, or _assessments/webwork-assignments/ in a course that has not moved)
# and fill it in. webwork-build reads it from there by default; -t names another,
# so a course can keep one template per kind of set -- practice, review, gateway.
#
# WHY A TEMPLATE. A topic repo records only which problems are in a set and in
# what order, so that another course can reuse it. Everything else in a .def
# belongs to a course and a term -- the dates, the set header, whether attempts
# are limited, what a problem is worth -- and lives here instead.
#
# Format: an ordinary .def, with three differences.
#
#   - Exactly ONE problem_start ... problem_end block. It is repeated once per
#     problem, in order, with {PROBLEM_ID} and {SOURCE_FILE} filled in. Any
#     field you add to it is repeated too.
#   - {PLACEHOLDERS}, filled in anywhere:
#       {SETID}        the set ID, e.g. OS1.1_Review_of_Functions
#       {SECTION}      the section prefix, e.g. OS1.1
#       {TITLE}        the title from the directory names, underscores as spaces
#       {HEADER}       the set header's path on the server, once copied in
#       {PROBLEM_ID}   1, 2, 3, ...                     (problem block only)
#       {SOURCE_FILE}  the problem's path on the server (problem block only)
#   - A `#! header: PATH' line names the set header, relative to the course
#     repo. It is COPIED into the set as 00-setHeader.pg, so a header kept in one
#     topic serves a set from any other. Leave it out, and write defaultHeader
#     instead of {HEADER}, to use the server's default.
#
# Every other #-comment line (like these) is dropped from the generated .def.
# Blank lines are kept.
#
# The fields below are those of MATH1003's OS1.2 practice set, written by hand
# before this script existed. The dates are EXAMPLES: replace every one.

#! header: 0-functions/webwork/local/set-headers/practice-setHeader.pg

assignmentType          = default
openDate                = 09/01/2026 at 01:00pm ADT
dueDate                 = 12/09/2026 at 05:00pm AST
answerDate              = 12/09/2026 at 07:00pm AST
enableReducedScoring    = N
paperHeaderFile         = {HEADER}
screenHeaderFile        = {HEADER}
description             = Practice for {SECTION} -- {TITLE}
restrictProbProgression = 0
emailInstructor         = 0

problemListV2
problem_start
problem_id           = {PROBLEM_ID}
source_file          = {SOURCE_FILE}
value                = 1
max_attempts         = -1
showMeAnother        = -1
showHintsAfter       = -2
prPeriod             = -1
counts_parent_grade  = 0
att_to_open_children = 0
problem_end
